    {
      "id": "A-DETAIL",
      "statement": "The shaft is oak of radius 0.04 m, running in a bore of radius 0.045 m through a turned oak pillar 0.56 m high and standing on an iron pivot in an iron step at the bottom of that bore. The four arms are turned oak in an oak hub; the balls sit on the arms' tenons. The crank on top follows the sheet; its size is ours. Bearing friction is not quantified.",
      "reason": "Complete the numerical modern demonstration without presenting invented details as Leonardo dimensions."
    }
