  "research": {
    "identification": "Madrid I114r [EL-FLY].",
    "sheet_vs_reconstruction": "Six motion arrangements and the relation between driving and driven bodies are discussed [EL-FLY]. Mario Taddei lists a flywheel reconstruction [FLY-M]. This four-weight stand is independent modern explanatory geometry. The sheet draws a crank on top of each shaft it tries, and the model has one there. The pillar, the step, the hub, the arms and their joinery are built as a workshop of the period would build them, and are ours.",
    "dimensions": "No explicit physical dimensions or Richter number verified [EL-FLY]. No braccio conversion made.",
    "claims": {
      "claimed_by_leonardo": "Leonardo compares balanced and unbalanced rotating weights and rejects the driven body as its own source [EL-FLY].",
      "tested_by_leonardo": "No dated experiment by Leonardo was verified in the sources listed here. This is an evidence gap, not proof that he never tried it.",
